      "text": "West Wood takes its name from the Westwood subdivision, a neighborhood located just west of Castleview Hospital.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Wood%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The land in West Wood was a sparsely populated rural area until the Westwood subdivision began development in 1975.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Wood%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Opening in 1980, Castleview Hospital brought a significant increase of new residents to the West Wood area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Wood%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pinnacle Canyon and Porphyry Bench, both part of the Wasatch Plateau, border West Wood to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Wood%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Pinnacle Creek and the privately owned Carbon Canal are the primary streams flowing through West Wood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
